/T (Network scanners and firewall matrices frequently export host-by-port state matricesin wide format \(one row per host, one column per monitored port\). While compact for visual inspection, wide matrices break relational joins and tidyverse filtering. Using tidyr::pivot_longer\(\) \(equivalent to reshape2::melt\(\)\), I designated host_ip and subnet_zone as identifier variables, port_number as the reshaped dimension variable, and port_state as the measured value variable. )
